{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"ORCHESTRATION STATUS (2026-08-13) — epic is CODE-COMPLETE; only the operator-dispatched live DC-harness run remains.\n\nChildren (5/6 closed):\n- brutal-dyable-lion (Cloud ADF codec): CLOSED\n- repressive-delectable-swan (DC wiki renderer): CLOSED\n- ashy-waterlog-hamadryas (DC robustness/perf): CLOSED\n- disparaged-parodistic-shrew (echo suppression + LWW conflict): CLOSED\n- emersed-specific-mutt (append-only comment sync): CLOSED this session — Gerrit change 1762 MERGED (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1); all 11 named AC tests pass.\n- dangerous-original-graywolf (live DC harness + contract test): IN_PROGRESS — code landed this session (Gerrit change 1766 MERGED, commit b6772e4f66, LLM-Review +1 / Verified +1). Its AC3 (normalize_rich_text cross-repo contract test, 10 tests) is DONE. Its AC1/AC2 are tagged [operator-attested] and left open because they are proven ONLY by the live Dockerized-Jira DC-harness job (tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_rich_text_live.py), which does not run on ordinary Gerrit changes.\n\nBlocking the epic close: the epic's own live-DC ACs (Docker Jira DC job exercises the cutover; rendered-HTML via expand=renderedFields; second pass performs no body update) and graywolf's AC1/AC2 all require the live 'Live External Integration' workflow (jira-dc-harness job). That workflow has NO dispatch inputs to narrow its matrix, so triggering it also runs the credentialed live-LLM arms (material provider spend), and the DC-harness job itself takes ~1h (downloads Jira 8.17.1 + boots a container). That paid/attested live run is an operator decision — not self-dispatched.\n\nTo finish: operator dispatches the live job (e.g. gh workflow run 'Live External Integration' --repo